<!-- wp_replay_meters.olx — the clock and the children meter for the replay.

     Referenced as <Use ref="wp_meters"/> at the top of every episode block
     (wp_ra … wp_rh, wp_rend). Display mode: both lines draw a computed
     position and are never written by the learner. sum() skips forks that
     have not been answered, so both lines start at their baseline and move
     only as choices are made. Nothing here locks.

     ======================================================================
     MACRO TABLE — the expression language has no let-bindings, so writers
     use these names in scripts and builders paste the expression verbatim.
     Copy from here; do not re-derive. Source of truth: notes/replay/CONTRACT.md.

     In an XML attribute, && must be written as &amp;&amp;. The table below
     is a comment, so it shows the plain source form.

     ALL_CODES  = @wp_ra1.code, @wp_ra2.code, @wp_rb1.code, @wp_rb2.code,
                  @wp_rb3.code, @wp_rc1.code, @wp_rc2.code, @wp_rd1.code,
                  @wp_rd2.code, @wp_re1.code, @wp_re2.code, @wp_rf1.code,
                  @wp_rf2.code, @wp_rg1.code, @wp_rg2.code, @wp_rg3.code,
                  @wp_rh1.code, @wp_rh2.code          (eighteen forks)

     MINUTE               Math.floor(10 + sum([ALL_CODES]) / 60)   (interpolate as {{MINUTE}})
     TICKET_AT            10 + sum([ALL_CODES]) / 60
     A_PRAISED            @wp_ra1.value === 'praise_next'
     A_PRESSED            @wp_ra1.value === 'press'
     A_WIDENED            @wp_ra1.value === 'widen'
     A_TO_AALIYAH         @wp_ra2.value === 'to_aaliyah'
     MARCUS_FIRST         @wp_ra2.value === 'press_again'
     MARCUS_CHARTED_WRONG @wp_ra2.value === 'chart'
     B_OUT                @wp_rb1.value === 'redirect'
     B_CHARTED            @wp_rb1.value === 'park'
     B_IN                 @wp_rb1.value === 'take_up'
     B_NAMED              @wp_rb2.value === 'name_it'
     B_PRESSED            @wp_rb2.value === 'press_science'
     B_ROOM               @wp_rb2.value === 'ask_room'
     B_BRIDGED            @wp_rb3.value === 'bridge'
     B_RUN                @wp_rb3.value === 'run'
     CHART_BIGGER         @wp_rb2.value === 'name_it' || @wp_rb2.value === 'press_science' || @wp_rb3.value === 'bridge'
     L3_SPENT             @wp_rb2.value === 'press_science' || @wp_rc1.value === 'answer'
     C_HELD               @wp_rc1.value === 'hold'
     C_ANSWERED           @wp_rc1.value === 'answer'
     C_ROOM               @wp_rc1.value === 'hand_to_room'
     DIEGO_RELAYED        @wp_rc1.value === 'hand_to_room'
     DIEGO_ASKED          @wp_rc2.value === 'ask_diego'
     KEISHA_EARLY         @wp_ra1.value === 'widen' || @wp_rb2.value === 'ask_room'
     E_TAKEN              @wp_rd1.value === 'jaylen'
     F_TAKEN              @wp_rd2.value === 'keisha'
     BOTH_TAKEN           @wp_rd1.value === 'jaylen' && @wp_rd2.value === 'keisha'
     E_OUT                @wp_re1.value === 'redirect'
     E_CHARTED            @wp_re1.value === 'park' || @wp_re2.value === 'distinction'
     E_RUN                @wp_re2.value === 'run'
     F_OUT                @wp_rf1.value === 'redirect' || @wp_rf2.value === 'correct'
     F_CHARTED            @wp_rf1.value === 'park' || @wp_rf2.value === 'chart_rule' || @wp_rf2.value === 'ask_ocean'
     F_RULE               @wp_rf1.value === 'take_up'
     QUIET_COUNT          (@wp_rb1.value === 'redirect' ? 1 : 0) + (@wp_re1.value === 'redirect' ? 1 : 0) + (@wp_rf1.value === 'redirect' ? 1 : 0) + (@wp_rc1.value === 'answer' ? 1 : 0)
     G_PREDICT            @wp_rg1.value === 'predict'
     G_WAITED             @wp_rg2.value === 'wait'
     G_REWROTE            @wp_rg3.value === 'rewrite'
     H_COLD               @wp_rh1.value === 'cold_call'
     H_VOLUNTEER          @wp_rh1.value === 'volunteer'
     MARCUS_OWNS_ROOM     @wp_ra2.value === 'press_again' && @wp_rh1.value === 'volunteer'
     DIEGO_WORD           @wp_rh1.value === 'together' || @wp_rh1.value === 'desk_check' || @wp_rh2.value === 'wait' || @wp_rh2.value === 'point'
     DIEGO_PASSED         @wp_rh2.value === 'rescue'
     PAST_20              10 + sum([ALL_CODES]) / 60 > 20
     PAST_22              10 + sum([ALL_CODES]) / 60 > 22

     Taken up, defined once (what the children meter counts; praised and used
     do not count):
       Marcus  = MARCUS_FIRST || A_TO_AALIYAH || MARCUS_CHARTED_WRONG || B_BRIDGED
       Aaliyah = B_CHARTED || B_IN
       Bri     = C_HELD || C_ROOM || B_PRESSED || B_BRIDGED
       Diego   = DIEGO_WORD || DIEGO_ASKED
       Jaylen  = E_CHARTED || E_RUN
       Keisha  = F_CHARTED || F_RULE
     ====================================================================== -->

<Vertical id="wp_meters">

<Collapsible id="wp_meters_howto" title="How the replay works">
<Markdown id="wp_meters_howto_md">
You're Ms. Boyd, from minute 10. At each fork, pick what you'd actually say. **The clock** moves with every choice (slides planned for 20, exit ticket for 30, bell at 45). **The second bar** counts children whose ideas you've *taken up*: built on, charted, or handed to the class; praise alone doesn't count. Twice, halfway and at the end, **a strip** shows where each child stands. No path takes up every child and still makes the exit ticket, so every choice is a trade.
</Markdown>
</Collapsible>

<NumberLineInput id="wp_clock" min="0" max="47" step="0.1" snap="step" display="true"
                 markerLabel="now"
                 placeholder="The clock starts when you make a move."
                 initial="10 + sum([@wp_ra1.code, @wp_ra2.code, @wp_rb1.code, @wp_rb2.code, @wp_rb3.code, @wp_rc1.code, @wp_rc2.code, @wp_rd1.code, @wp_rd2.code, @wp_re1.code, @wp_re2.code, @wp_rf1.code, @wp_rf2.code, @wp_rg1.code, @wp_rg2.code, @wp_rg3.code, @wp_rh1.code, @wp_rh2.code]) / 60">
  <Tick value="10" label="share-out"   > share-out   </Tick>
  <Tick value="20" label="slides"      > slides      </Tick>
  <Tick value="30" label="exit ticket" > exit ticket </Tick>
  <Tick value="45" label="bell"        > bell        </Tick>
</NumberLineInput>

<NumberLineInput id="wp_children" min="0" max="6" step="1" snap="step" display="true"
                 markerLabel="taken up"
                 initial="Math.min(6, (@wp_ra2.value === 'press_again' || @wp_ra2.value === 'to_aaliyah' || @wp_ra2.value === 'chart' || @wp_rb3.value === 'bridge' ? 1 : 0) + (@wp_rb1.value === 'park' || @wp_rb1.value === 'take_up' ? 1 : 0) + (@wp_rc1.value === 'hold' || @wp_rc1.value === 'hand_to_room' || @wp_rb2.value === 'press_science' || @wp_rb3.value === 'bridge' ? 1 : 0) + (@wp_rh1.value === 'together' || @wp_rh1.value === 'desk_check' || @wp_rh2.value === 'wait' || @wp_rh2.value === 'point' || @wp_rc2.value === 'ask_diego' ? 1 : 0) + (@wp_re1.value === 'park' || @wp_re2.value === 'distinction' || @wp_re2.value === 'run' ? 1 : 0) + (@wp_rf1.value === 'park' || @wp_rf2.value === 'chart_rule' || @wp_rf2.value === 'ask_ocean' || @wp_rf1.value === 'take_up' ? 1 : 0))">
  <Tick value="0" label="none"    > none    </Tick>
  <Tick value="6" label="all six" > all six </Tick>
</NumberLineInput>

<!-- ROSTER STRIP: moved out at the October 27 review ("remove the section on
     who is participating in which block. Maybe use two instances of the
     participation pattern"). It used to sit here, under the two bars, on every
     episode. It now lives, unchanged, in wp_replay_roster.olx and is shown
     twice: at the top of Five hands (wp_rd, halfway) and of The pile (wp_rend,
     the end). To put it back on every episode, add <Use ref="wp_roster_strip"/>
     here and remove those two Uses. -->

</Vertical>
